gb4W(){return"Length, elevation and the difficulty as your network sees it \u2014 a tap on the grade shows who rated it how."},
gb4F(){return"Color means difficulty"},
gb4E(){return"Every line carries its trail\u2019s difficulty like a ski run. The style of the line tells its condition: crumbly means worn, dashed means beaten up, faded means barely rideable. An orange edge is a warning (closed, destroyed, changed), a yellow one shows a new report from a buddy. The legend on the left edge opens and closes at any time."},
gb4L(){return"What the map shows"},
